  "resolution": "Finite satisfiable observation entailment reuses ConclusivelyVerifiable, one empirical proof standard. Arbitrary semantic consequence from given premises is separate; neither is independently warranted demonstration or every theological proof. The q46a2 world-beginning source statement is not redefined or claimed proved. Subject, presented revelation premises and declared method are independent typed domain criteria, not theological:=unverifiable. Every named class has a proof-positive tautology in the control. Selected beginning restriction is separate and not all theology. T→ObservationBarrier is explicit before restricted proof denial follows. Existing Norm.selfApplication applies to a real metaclaim only with its actual scope/representation witness; no automatic theological self-membership follows. Named domain/barrier coverage stay open, with explicit genuine remaining-domain and additional-barrier alternatives. Hume Assessment theology withholding is an entitlement verdict, not a proof-impossibility theorem. See docs/notes/scoped-empirical-proof-barrier.md.",
